---
description: SQLAlchemy sessions, repositories, queries, and Alembic
globs: backend/app/core/database.py,backend/**/models.py,backend/**/repository.py,backend/alembic/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the session factory in `app/core/database.py`. Do not create engines or
session factories inside modules. Async SQLAlchemy only. No synchronous
session use in request handlers.

One business operation has one transaction boundary. Do not commit from
unrelated layers for the same operation. Do not hold a transaction across a
slow external or model call.

Repositories own queries and persistence mapping. Filter every
organization-owned table by `organization_id` from the authenticated
context.

Load relationships intentionally. Avoid N+1 queries and extra round trips
that the caller does not need.

Schema changes go through Alembic. Do not edit models without a migration,
and do not rewrite a migration that may already have been applied.
